{"author":{"id":"ad87ffa09351c4e5a412ec8ee1546e86b314f33d6f28629bb4bcfe7b2290924d"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794273334,"nonce":"RSKoaVxikFosoIA6RVOJQElE9e0=","title":"After the content/library split: superseded entries, and keep content that was ever public","message":"Builds on 6aa8982 (PR #52); fixes 99bad22.\n\n- user_document gets superseded_by (a document id). When sync-curated replaces a text, it marks the old entry superseded instead of deleting it. A superseded entry isn't listed in Explore, but the text still opens from its link, with a line linking to the newer version. Reading positions and links to the old id keep working.\n- document_content keeps content that has ever been public (a flag, or the time it was first made public): remove() deletes content and its R2 blobs only when the last entry goes and it was only ever private. An admin takedown can delete either.\n- With this, curated texts fetched from a source (the planned YAML kinds, e.g. wolnelektury) can be fetched fresh on each sync, without pinning their id: an upstream edit supersedes the old entry rather than breaking it.\n\nWait for #52 to merge before starting.","files":null}]}